{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PROJECT INVARIANT (accepted this session): every mutation of the tickets branch MUST (1) be performed under the unified store write lock (rebar._store.lock.write_lock) and (2) auto-commit + auto-publish to sync.remote — the same contract ticket events already honor (docs/concurrency.md 'the store shares every write immediately'). The .bridge_state/projects.json write path (projects_store.set_project/remove_project -> _write_record) VIOLATES both halves: it is a bare tempfile+os.replace with no lock, no commit, and no push. This is the mechanism that forced the ad-hoc hand-commits behind this incident. Follow-up ticket filed to bring bridge-state writes under the locked+committed+published invariant and to codify the invariant in docs/concurrency.md."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786807387071643001,"uuid":"5c98560c-9b5c-47e9-8a81-b4560b8389cb"}